Problem:
A university has a car building fundraiser where students build toy cars and toy trucks using wheels and wood and sell to benefit a nearby shelter. A toy car requires 4 wheels and 7 units of wood while a toy truck requires 6 wheels and 10 units of wood. Each team has at most 40 wheels and 75 units of wood. In addition, each team can build at most 3 toy cars and the number of toy trucks must be larger than the number toy cars. If a toy car can fundraise $30 and a toy truck can fundraise $35, how many of each toy should a team build to maximize the total amount fundraised?

Model and facts:
